{"title":"Career Roadmap · Rehabilitation Specialist","role":"Rehabilitation Specialist","summary":"A Rehabilitation Specialist works with patients recovering from injury, surgery, neurological conditions, chronic diseases, disability, or functional limitations. The role focuses on restoring mobility, strength, balance, independence, physical function, and quality of life.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Physiotherapy (BPT)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Rehabilitation Specialist works with patients recovering from injury, surgery, neurological conditions, chronic diseases, disability, or functional limitations. The role focuses on restoring mobility, strength, balance, independence, physical function, and quality of life."},{"type":"p","text":"For the BPT pathway, the strongest foundation is a Bachelor of Physiotherapy (BPT) followed by clinical internship and focused experience. For advanced specialist or academic roles, MPT or another relevant postgraduate qualification can provide deeper specialization."},{"type":"p","text":"A Rehabilitation Specialist may work across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Sports rehabilitation clinics"},{"text":"Neurological rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Orthopaedic centres"},{"text":"Geriatric care"},{"text":"Home healthcare"},{"text":"Occupational rehabilitation"},{"text":"Disability rehabilitation"},{"text":"Community rehabilitation"},{"text":"Digital/remote rehabilitation"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"BPT fundamentals, anatomy, physiology, biomechanics, exercise therapy and clinical exposure"}],[{"text":"2030–2034"},{"text":"Clinical internship → Physio